EXAMPLES=[{'num':'5','title':'Trapezoid Integral and Error','question':'Approximate ∫₋₁²x² dx with four trapezoidal subintervals and compare with the exact integral.','steps':['Set a=−1,b=2,N=4 and h=(b−a)/N=3/4.','Nodes are −1,−1/4,1/2,5/4,2. Their squares are 1,1/16,1/4,25/16,4.','Apply T₄=(h/2)[f₀+2(f₁+f₂+f₃)+f₄].','The weighted sum is 1+2(1/16+1/4+25/16)+4=35/4=8.75.','Thus T₄=(3/8)(35/4)=105/32=3.28125.','The exact integral [x³/3]₋₁²=3. Signed error exact minus approximate is −9/32=−0.28125, an overestimate.','Since x² is convex, trapezoid chords lie above the curve, independently confirming the sign of the error.'],'answer':'T₄=3.28125; exact I=3; signed error I−T₄=−0.28125.','progressiveSolution':True,'solutionOrigin':'SpaceBook learning enhancement','sourceReferences':[{'page':319,'jpg':'164_page_1.jpg','verification':'All sample fractions, weighted sum and signed error checked'}]}]

